<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · artifact</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hiawatha Belt</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hiawatha">Hiawatha</a> Belt is a wampum belt of purple and white shell <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bead">beads</a> that records the founding of the Haudenosaunee (Iroquois) Confederacy. Its four squares and central tree stand for the five original nations, linked by a line, with the Onondaga, keepers of the central council fire, at the centre. It is a principal symbol of the confederacy, and its design serves as the Haudenosaunee flag.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hiawatha-belt.jpg" alt="Hiawatha Belt" width="320" height="251" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Thomas Eakins · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hiawatha_-_Eakins.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
